      "content": "Then let the story end. There's no rule that says you have to keep turning pages just because they're blank. You've given everything you had, and that's a complete, honest life—nothing to be ashamed of. But if you're truly done, then stop pretending, stop forcing the motion. Just sit in that emptiness and let it be what it is. Maybe that's not the end—maybe it's just the first time you've let yourself be still without a purpose. And if it is the end, at least you'll have faced it with your eyes open.",
